{
    "word": "chervil",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7012b154-f3b5-3993-a1d1-7768f9d81013",
                "word": "chervil",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1cdd1cc4-3267-4120-b1dc-b66e09176abd",
                        "entry_id": "7012b154-f3b5-3993-a1d1-7768f9d81013",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "chervils"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "66c15510-7297-3825-b39c-2d4630db4748",
                        "entry_id": "7012b154-f3b5-3993-a1d1-7768f9d81013",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A leafy herb, Anthriscus cerefolium, resembling parsley."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b65ec751-90e4-4bd4-8bb1-3e877a11b34f",
                                "sense_id": "66c15510-7297-3825-b39c-2d4630db4748",
                                "text": "The life of one plant would be affected by another. Rue was definitely hostile to basil, rosemary to hyssop, but coriander, dill and chervil lived on the friendliest of terms[.]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5ace4594-4ac9-3fa8-9d42-6a6a92ee18e9",
                        "entry_id": "7012b154-f3b5-3993-a1d1-7768f9d81013",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Leaves from the plant, used as an herb in cooking, which have a mild flavor of anise."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c68cfb8b-b84e-4ae0-bc90-f5f1b35de37c",
                                "sense_id": "5ace4594-4ac9-3fa8-9d42-6a6a92ee18e9",
                                "text": "No herb, except perhaps tarragon, is quite so French as chervil, an association that is not surprising for a nation known for its celebration of fine food and the subtle use of herbs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c09327a4-194b-4f10-81d7-60ebbc059b6c",
                                "sense_id": "5ace4594-4ac9-3fa8-9d42-6a6a92ee18e9",
                                "text": "Cook fresh chervil leaves very little, if at all. They are best when added to a dish after it has been cooked, or toward the end of the cooking time."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ec98684c-647b-4b56-bd8f-22545b1b1708",
                        "source_entry_id": "7012b154-f3b5-3993-a1d1-7768f9d81013",
                        "source_sense_description": "plant",
                        "target_lang_word": "cerfeuil",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cerfeuil",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af013a07-1cb3-309a-8fff-a134e6cd8f76",
                                        "entry_id": "00189bad-5899-3376-9391-5db196abc42a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Plante potagère annuelle aromatique de la famille des Apiacées (ou Ombellifères) qui est employée dans la cuisine comme assaisonnement ou comme ingrédient dans des potages et dont le nom scientifique est Anthriscus cerefolium (L.) Hoffm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4b72d4a-9052-4cc2-bd28-7b3a7d661551",
                                                "sense_id": "af013a07-1cb3-309a-8fff-a134e6cd8f76",
                                                "text": "Plante herbacée annuelle au feuillage triangulaire, léger et finement dentelé, le cerfeuil est indigène du sud-est de l’Europe et du Caucase, en Asie centrale."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8457c9ca-ab5f-3ca4-b7d7-f0cb9bbf5000",
                                        "entry_id": "00189bad-5899-3376-9391-5db196abc42a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nom donné à d'autres Apiacées que Anthriscus cerefolium citée au dessus, notamment de nombreuses plantes du genre Chaerophyllum dont certaines sont comestibles (par ex.cerfeuil tubéreux) et d'autres toxiques (par ex. cerfeuil des fous)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "460ca973-4965-3d47-877f-5492abde66c7",
                                        "entry_id": "00189bad-5899-3376-9391-5db196abc42a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nom donné à d'autres Apiacées que Anthriscus cerefolium citée en premier, notamment à Myrrhis odorata connu sous les noms de cerfeuil musqué, cerfeuil anisé ou cerfeuil d'Espagne qui est une plante comestible."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
